NDIP-3 A2 mutation-plan record envelope correction
Date: 2026-10-04
Base commit: 8e6da8cf4245f43203f699665c53f83da16e9e82

Source-derived bound:
  readyProjections considers at most 3 affected Lanes and reads each Lane value
  twice. For each Lane, DUE and ORDERED each visit at most one removed Timeline
  row and one retained row, and validate at most one candidate Message. For a
  legacy Message without TimelineWorkRef, actionAtFor may additionally scan
  L = max(maxPendingMessages, maxOutcomeReserveRecords) open Attempt records,
  then read its ScheduleBinding and the Message referenced by that binding.
  NATIVE visits at most 2 Timeline rows and reads one candidate Message.
  Thus the stored candidates and Lane reads use at most
  3 * (2 + 2 * (L + 5) + 3) = 6L + 45 records.

  The included replacement Message and excluded prior Message can each require
  one additional legacy actionAt lookup, each bounded by L Attempt records plus
  2 ScheduleBinding/Message reads. The full plan bound is therefore
  6L + 45 + 2 * (L + 2) = 8L + 49 records. Default config has L=4,000,000,
  so activation requires at least 32,000,049 records. The initial 33-record
  calculation omitted legacy scans; the intermediate 7L+47 calculation also
  omitted the included replacement lookup. Both were incomplete.

Change:
  HeadReadPolicy derives the record allowance from DelayShardConfig with
  overflow-safe arithmetic. Active Owner activation rejects policies below this
  bound. DelayShard reuses actionAt for each stored candidate's key and
  projection. The activation regression checks the default derived value and
  rejects one record below it. This covers only the record dimension; variable
  value bytes/allocation, production byte/time policy assembly, and central
  validation remain open. A2 remains IN_PROGRESS.

